---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
---

<SubpageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms and conditions governing the use of StructZero platform, web interface, and MCP server integrations."
  status="Official Spec"
  summary="StructZero provides multi-agent software engineering orchestration, model context protocol servers, and deployment connectors under these binding terms."
  related={[
    { label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/legal/privacy' },
    { label: 'Acceptable Use Policy', href: '/legal/acceptable-use' },
    { label: 'Security Policy', href: '/legal/security-policy' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-10 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
    <section class="border-b border-border/50 pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing the StructZero platform, connecting via Model Context Protocol (MCP), or utilizing our web interfaces, you ("Customer" or "User") agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you are entering into these terms on behalf of a company or organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that entity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border/50 pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">2. Description of Platform & Services</h2>
      <p>
        StructZero is an AI Software Engineering Platform that coordinates autonomous multi-agent councils, Project DNA codebase indexing, multi-model debate, automated certification release gates, and cloud deployment connectors (AWS, Vercel, GCP, Azure).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border/50 pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">3. Human Authorization Guardrails & User Responsibility</h2>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 text-sm text-amber-300 font-medium mb-4">
        <strong>Authorization Control:</strong> StructZero incorporates explicit human authorization intercepts for billable cloud infrastructure provisioning and destructive execution commands.
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>The Customer retains ultimate responsibility for reviewing and approving operations.</strong> StructZero is not liable for cloud charges incurred from user-approved executions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border/50 pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">4. Proprietary Rights & Customer Code Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Customer retains all right, title, and interest in and to all source code, software architecture designs, data models, and artifacts generated or modified by StructZero during your utilization of the platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border/50 pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">5. Service Level Agreement (SLA) & Availability</h2>
      <p>
        StructZero provides platform availability targets of 99.9% uptime for cloud control plane APIs. Hosting deployments deployed by StructZero inherit the underlying SLAs of the targeted cloud provider (Vercel, AWS, GCP, Azure).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">6. Limitation of Liability & Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        Platform services are provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. StructZero's maximum aggregate liability shall not exceed the total fees paid by Customer to StructZero in the twelve (12) months preceding the claim.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</SubpageLayout>
